<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>FADE IN:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. LOGGING ROAD - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dense Alaskan forest, black on black. A single pair of headlights crawl along a gravel switchback.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A LOG TRUCK, overloaded, groans under its own weight.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. LOG TRUCK - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>JIM (25, lean, patchy beard, a knit cap he never takes off) drives with one hand, eating sunflower seeds with the other. Shells pile in the cupholder.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>DOG (34, broad, quiet, hands scarred across the knuckles) rides shotgun. Stares out the window like he&#x27;s counting trees.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You ever think about how we&#x27;re basically just moving really expensive firewood around all night?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog says nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That&#x27;s the whole job. Felt that way to you? Ever?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Non.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>&quot;Non.&quot; You&#x27;re French now?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Watch the road.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Somewhere out in the dark treeline --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>KNOCK.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim&#x27;s head snaps toward the sound. Dog doesn&#x27;t move, but his jaw tightens.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...The hell was that.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quiet)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A beat. Then --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>KNOCK. KNOCK.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog sits up straight now, scanning the treeline hard.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That ain&#x27;t nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(low, urgent)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Pull over.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>We got a schedule, man, Walt&#x27;s gonna --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>PULL OVER.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim pulls over. Cuts the engine. Silence floods in.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(trying to joke through it)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Scale of one to ten, how worried should I be right now.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(dead serious)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Four.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Four&#x27;s not that bad.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Four&#x27;s bad enough.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog opens his door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. LOGGING ROAD - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog steps out, flashlight up, scanning the treeline. Jim follows, seeds still in hand, trying to look braver than he feels.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What&#x27;s two knocks mean? Is there a glossary? &#x27;Cause one knock I got, that&#x27;s like a &quot;hello,&quot; but two --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Two means we&#x27;re already late.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Late for what.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog doesn&#x27;t answer. He&#x27;s listening.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A THIRD KNOCK -- closer. Much closer. Right behind the truck.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim and Dog turn as one.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Nothing there. Just dark.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Then the GROUND SHUDDERS. Something massive moves through the treeline, unseen, shaking needles loose from the canopy.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The truck&#x27;s load of logs SHIFTS violently --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MOVE --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He shoves Jim clear as the entire load tips, logs crashing down across the cab in an avalanche of timber and sound. The truck folds like a beer can.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Silence after. Steam hisses from the crushed engine block.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim, on the ground, staring at the wreck.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(small voice)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...Four was generous.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>CUT TO:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. TRAPPER&#x27;S CABIN - NIGHT (INSERT - FLASHBACK, 1966)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Grainy, high-contrast. A YOUNG DOG (25) crouches in the doorway of this same cabin, rifle shaking in his hands. We don&#x27;t see what he&#x27;s aiming at -- just his face, pure terror.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A GUNSHOT.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Something roars -- pained, massive, ancient.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>BACK TO SCENE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. LOGGING ROAD - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog, present day, staring at the wreck, breathing hard. The flashback lives behind his eyes for just a second too long.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You good?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(snapping back)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>We walk from here.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Walk WHERE. It&#x27;s the middle of the night and something just ate our truck.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>There&#x27;s a crossing. Four miles. Ford across the river. Radio works from the ranger box on the other side.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Four miles through THAT.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(points into the trees)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What even hit us?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog starts walking. Doesn&#x27;t answer.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(following, to himself)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Cool. Cool cool cool. Love that for us.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. FOREST TRAIL - NIGHT - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: 12:14 AM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim and Dog move single file, flashlights cutting thin lines through fog. Jim keeps glancing at the trees.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>So back there -- the knocks. You knew what that was before it hit us.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Didn&#x27;t know it&#x27;d hit us.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>But you knew SOMETHING.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog keeps walking.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Dog. Come on. You&#x27;ve been doing this route longer than me. You flinched before anything even happened.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(finally)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>There&#x27;s a toll. Been one longer than either of us worked here.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>A toll. Like a bridge toll.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Like a bridge toll that eats trucks if you don&#x27;t pay it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(trying to laugh)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Okay, so who do we make the check out to --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(sharp)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I&#x27;m serious, Jim.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim stops laughing. Dog rarely raises his voice.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...Okay. Who pays it. Walt?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long pause. Too long.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I do.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You pay it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Every June. Have for nine years.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(processing)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That&#x27;s... that&#x27;s not in the job description, man.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No. It&#x27;s not.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog walks faster. Jim has to jog to keep up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Did I -- wait. Did something happen with THIS year&#x27;s --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog says nothing. That&#x27;s answer enough.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quiet, sick realization)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I used the toll money. In June. I was short for the truck payment, I figured --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I figured it was just, like, Walt&#x27;s beer fund or something, I didn&#x27;t --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(flat)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You didn&#x27;t pay it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I paid HALF. Last year I paid half, nothing bad happened --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Last year wasn&#x27;t nothing. Last year was a warning.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog stops walking. Turns to face him fully for the first time.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>This is the second notice.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Off Jim&#x27;s face -- the real fear setting in --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>CUT TO:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. FOREST TRAIL - NIGHT - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: 12:36 AM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They walk in silence now. Fog thickens. Jim&#x27;s flashlight flickers.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(trying to fill silence)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Scale of one to ten.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Six.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Six?! It was FOUR twenty minutes ago!</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Twenty minutes ago you hadn&#x27;t told me you stole the toll.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They keep walking. Somewhere distant -- a KNOCK. Single. Both of them freeze.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(whispering)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>One knock&#x27;s a hello, right? You said hello --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(whispering back)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Said hello&#x27;s one knock. Didn&#x27;t say who&#x27;s saying it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They move again, faster now, flashlights jittering across the trees.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. FOREST TRAIL - BOG - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: 1:20 AM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The trail disappears into standing black water between dead, bone-white trees. A rope line -- old, half-rotted -- is strung between trunks, marking a path through the bog.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Please tell me that&#x27;s not the only way across.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It&#x27;s not the only way. It&#x27;s the way that doesn&#x27;t kill you.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They start across, following the rope hand over hand. The water is utterly still. Too still.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Halfway across, Jim&#x27;s flashlight catches something under the surface -- a shape, long and pale, gone before he can process it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Did you --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Don&#x27;t look at the water. Look at the rope.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I saw something --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(hard)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>LOOK AT THE ROPE, JIM.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim fixes his eyes forward. Keeps moving. His hand finds the rope, white-knuckled.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Behind them, the water doesn&#x27;t ripple -- but something tracks their movement beneath it, a wake with no source.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They reach the far side. Jim collapses onto solid ground, breathing hard.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What was that.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Don&#x27;t know. Don&#x27;t ask it questions either. Starts thinking you&#x27;re interested.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(half-laughing, panicked)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I&#x27;m not INTERESTED, I&#x27;m TERRIFIED, there&#x27;s a difference --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog&#x27;s already walking. Jim scrambles up to follow.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. FOREST TRAIL - NIGHT - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: 2:15 AM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The trail narrows. Trees close in overhead, blotting out what little moon there was.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nine years, Dog.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(not stopping)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Don&#x27;t.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I&#x27;m not trying to -- I just -- why didn&#x27;t you ever tell anybody. Tell WALT. Tell somebody who could help carry that.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(turning, sudden, raw)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Because I&#x27;m the one who shot it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Silence. Jim stares at him.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...What?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nineteen sixty-six. I was twenty-five. Thought it was a bear in the trap line. Wasn&#x27;t a bear.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You shot --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(gesturing vaguely at the forest)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>-- THAT?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Grazed it. Forehead. It&#x27;s got the scar to prove it, if you ever get close enough to see, which I&#x27;m praying to God you don&#x27;t.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>And the toll&#x27;s -- what, an apology? For forty years?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quiet)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Some debts don&#x27;t get paid off. They get paid DOWN. Every year. Forever, maybe. I don&#x27;t know. Nobody tells you the terms. You just find out when you miss a payment.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He starts walking again. Jim, shaken, follows.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. TRAPPER&#x27;S CABIN - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: 2:40 AM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A sagging, moss-covered cabin emerges from the fog -- the same cabin from the 1966 flashback, decades older now.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Please tell me this has a radio.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It&#x27;s got shelter. Storm&#x27;s coming in behind us. We wait it out, then we cross the ford at first light.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog pushes the door open. It groans.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. TRAPPER&#x27;S CABIN - NIGHT - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dust. A single busted window lets in gray moonlight. Jim sweeps his flashlight across the room --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>-- and stops on the walls.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Every surface is carved. Names. Numbers. Hash marks stacked in columns like a ledger no one asked for.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(flashlight scanning, can&#x27;t help himself)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Hollis... nineteen thirty-one.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat, moving the light)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Pruitt -- Jesus, fifty-nine to seventy-three. That&#x27;s not a toll, that&#x27;s a mortgage --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He keeps moving down the wall, narrating out of nerves more than curiosity -- the way he fills silence when he&#x27;s scared.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Looks like everybody who ever dropped a saw in this forest owes somebody something --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He stops.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dead center of the wall -- a single carved line, deeper than the rest, like it was cut in anger:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>DOG -- &#x27;66</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim&#x27;s flashlight holds on it. He doesn&#x27;t say anything.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He turns to Dog, who hasn&#x27;t moved from the doorway. Who clearly already knew it was there.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM (CONT&#x27;D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quiet, no joke left in it)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...Oh.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(not looking at the wall)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Non.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I didn&#x27;t ask anything.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You were gonna.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog steps past him, deeper into the cabin, like the wall doesn&#x27;t exist. Jim lowers the flashlight. Doesn&#x27;t push it. Not yet.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He sits against the wall opposite the carvings, pulls his knees up. Tries, for once, to just be quiet.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>It doesn&#x27;t last.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Can I ask you something that&#x27;s not about the wall.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(sitting, wary)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Depends.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>If it doesn&#x27;t give something back for free -- the forest, the toll, whatever this is -- what DOES it take? Like, in the worst case. What&#x27;s the actual price.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dog looks at him for a long moment. This is the first time he actually considers answering fully.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It don&#x27;t give nothing back for free. You want breath, you trade something that uses it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Cryptic. Cool. Love a good riddle at --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(checks nothing, has no watch)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>-- whatever time it is.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DOG</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>2:40.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JIM</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>2:40. Cool.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jim pulls his cap down over his eyes, trying to rest. Dog stays upright, alert, watching the door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Outside, faint and far off -- a single KNOCK. Neither of them reacts this time. They&#x27;re past reacting to one.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>FADE OUT.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>END OF PART ONE.</Text></Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>